  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Holistic emergency and long-term support for the impacted camps with disaster risk reduction measures in northwest Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome P&#xA0;- Camps are more accessible by humanitarian aid, ambulances and IDPs:&#xA0;Access to the camps by humanitarian aid, ambulances and IDPs is improved through efficient rainwater drainage and camp infrastructure enhancements.

Outcome Q - Women can access basic healthcare in 3 centres in NWS.&#xA0;The operations of 3 Women healthcare centres are supported to provide basic health services in the impacted camps for 9 months.


Outcome R - Communities are more prepared to respond to climate shocks:&#xA0;5 forecast climate data devices and systems are installed to enable and promote preparedness and response to climate shocks in northwest Syria</narrative>
  </description>
